  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1008 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nSunday begins a warming trend as weak ridging persists aloft and \nsouthwesterly surface flow continues to intensify. Models are now \nin good agreement keeping a series of upper level disturbances \nwell to our west through the first half of the week, which keeps \nprecipitation chances near zero over West TX through at least \nTuesday. Temperatures will also steadily warm throughout the week \nas as a ~590dam ridge axis builds over the region. This will \nresult in several days of temperatures near and above average with\ndaily highs in the mid 70s Mon-Tue and upper 70s to low 80s Wed-\nFri. Models then diverge regarding the evolution of the upper \nlevel pattern late in the week with differences in how quickly the\nbroad upper level troughing shifts eastward. Depending on how \nquickly this occurs, showers may return to the forecast area \nduring the Wed-Fri timeframe.",
